Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 18:36:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Duplication: a copy gets a name nothing else is using
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

This is the same incident as yesterday's "Your latest changes could not be
saved. Please retry before starting the test survey." Two questions exporting
the same variable is a blocking problem at the publish gate — it is the
fixture I used to test that refusal — so the survey could not be versioned,
and the Studio rendered the refusal as a vanishing toast that said retry.
Retrying could never work, because the duplicate name was still there.

THE CAUSE

Both duplicate paths appended `_COPY` unconditionally:

    copy.code = `${q.code}_COPY`;
    copy.variableName = `${q.variableName}_COPY`;

Duplicating a copy was fine — Q1_COPY becomes Q1_COPY_COPY. Duplicating the
SAME question twice was not: both copies are Q1_COPY, in both the code and the
variable name. Reproduced before fixing, and the block path did the same thing
once per question in the block.

THE FIX

`usedNames(def)` collects every name that already means something — question
codes AND variable names, calculation targets, embedded-data fields and the
reserved system columns. Codes and variable names are one namespace because
`getQuestionByCodeOrVar` resolves both, so a copy whose code lands on another
question's variable name is just as broken as two identical variable names,
and a check that looks at only one of them finds half the collisions.

`copyNames(taken, q)` then picks the first free suffix — `_COPY`, `_COPY_2`,
`_COPY_3` — applying the SAME one to the code and the variable name. They are
usually identical and a programmer expects them to stay in step, so numbering
them independently would be its own small betrayal. The block path shares one
`taken` set across the whole block, because the copies are minted before any
of them is in the definition.

WHAT WAS ALREADY CORRECT, AND IS UNCHANGED

Requirements 2, 3 and 4 of the report — manual renaming, propagation, and
refusing a name that is taken — are already built and working.
`VariableNameInput` is wired into the question editor and the calculation
editor and goes through `renameImpact` + `applyRename`, which rewrite every
reference (logic, conditions, piping, calculations, randomisers, embedded
data, validation) and refuse a collision, a reserved column, an invalid
identifier or a name that shadows a calc function. I verified this rather than
rebuilding it, and added tests pinning both behaviours so they stay true.

So the "variable name shown in the editor is the single source of truth"
requirement was already met on the editing path; it was only duplication that
could create a second question claiming the same name behind the programmer's
back.

11 tests. Three mutations — the blind append, dropping codes from the
namespace, and numbering the two fields independently — each caught, the last
two only after the first versions of those tests proved too weak to tell the
difference. 15 packages and typecheck green.

